    {
      "id": "0be262ce0634-q2",
      "number": 2,
      "question": "Which of the following is the correct relationship? &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following is the correct relationship?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "F = a/m F = a/m",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">F = a/m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">F = a/m</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "F = m/a F = m/a",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">F = m/a</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">F = m/a</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "F = m2a F = m2a",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">F = m2a</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">F = m2a</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "F = ma F = ma",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">F = ma</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">F = ma</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>&#183; According to Newton's Second Law of Motion: Force (F) = mass (m)  X  acceleration (a).</p><p>&#183; This is a fundamental principle in physics.</p><p>&#183; This relationship shows that the force acting on an object is directly proportional to its mass and the acceleration it experiences.</p>",
