      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0be262ce0634-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "Which of the following is NOT an example of inertia at rest? &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2342;&#2366;&#2361;&#2352;&#2339; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following is NOT an example of inertia at rest?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2342;&#2366;&#2361;&#2352;&#2339; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Falling down backward when a vehicle starts immediately &#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2344; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354;&#2370; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2368;&#2331;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2323;&#2352; &#2327;&#2367;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Falling down backward when a vehicle starts immediately</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2344; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354;&#2370; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2368;&#2331;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2323;&#2352; &#2327;&#2367;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Falling down of dust particle while dusting a cloth &#2325;&#2346;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2343;&#2370;&#2354; &#2333;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2343;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2327;&#2367;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Falling down of dust particle while dusting a cloth</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2346;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2343;&#2370;&#2354; &#2333;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2343;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2327;&#2367;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "The detachment of leaves/fruits due to shaking &#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2346;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306;/&#2347;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">The detachment of leaves/fruits due to shaking</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2346;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306;/&#2347;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "The sudden application of brakes in a vehicle &#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2330;&#2366;&#2344;&#2325; &#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2325; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">The sudden application of brakes in a vehicle</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2330;&#2366;&#2344;&#2325; &#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2325; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>Inertia at rest (also known as inertia of rest) is the tendency of an object to remain in its state of rest. Options a, b, and c are examples of inertia of rest.</p><p><b>Option d, The sudden application of brakes in a vehicle</b> is an example of <b>inertia of motion</b>. When brakes are applied suddenly, the vehicle (and the lower part of the passengers' bodies in contact with it) comes to rest, but due to inertia of motion, the upper part of the passengers' bodies tends to continue moving forward.</p><p><b>Explanation of Other Options (Examples of Inertia of Rest):</b></p><p>&#8226; Falling down backward when a vehicle starts immediately: When a vehicle starts suddenly, the lower part of a passenger's body in contact with the vehicle moves forward, but the upper part, due to inertia of rest, tends to remain at rest, causing the passenger to fall backward.</p><p>&#8226; Falling down of dust particle while dusting a cloth: When a cloth (like a carpet) is beaten with a stick, the cloth is set into motion, but the dust particles, due to inertia of rest, tend to remain in their position of rest and thus get separated from the moving cloth.</p><p>&#8226; The detachment of leaves/fruits due to shaking: When a tree branch is shaken vigorously, the branch moves, but the leaves/fruits, due to inertia of rest, tend to remain at rest and thus get detached.</p><p><b>Further insights:</b></p><p>&#8226; Inertia is the property of matter by which it continues in its existing state of rest or uniform motion in a straight line, unless that state is changed by an external force.</p><p>&#8226; There are three types of inertia: inertia of rest, inertia of motion, and inertia of direction.</p><p>&#8226; Inertia of motion is the tendency of an object to remain in its state of uniform motion.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
